# Secure Coding Standards — {{project_name}}

<!-- GEN: Why: the non-negotiables and the workspace's security model must be visible while coding, not only at review. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->
<!-- GEN: Description: follow ~/.claude/skill-factory/core/authoring-guide.md "Description" — workspace name, concrete situations, the team's own trigger words (their language allowed), an "even if" clause; check it against the trial prompts (Step 8). -->

## Non-negotiables

1. Validate untrusted input at the boundary; reject, do not guess.
2. Authorize every operation on the server, per object; deny by default. UI hiding is UX only.
3. Every query, cache key, file path and job carries its scope ({{scope_list}}).
4. No string-built SQL, shell, template or path from input.
5. No secrets or personal data in code, logs, URLs, client bundles or error messages.
6. Fail closed: an error in validation or authorization denies.

